	ommp81PlusOduLossOfFrameLossOfMultiframeAlarm OBJECT-TYPE
              SYNTAX  DisplayString
              MAX-ACCESS  read-only
              STATUS  current
              DESCRIPTION
			"While demultiplexing the incoming OPU2 frame into the
			ODU1, if the start of a ODU1 frame is not found	then 
			this alarm is generated. Since the alarm is generated at
			the demultiplexing level, the alarm cannot be
			represented with respect to a client/line port, as one
			ODU1 slice might have multiple client data. This
			property is w.r.t slice
			-----------------------------
			ommp81PlusInterfaceNumber:
			ODU1 slices demapped from OTU2 signal received at LINE-1
			5 - ODU1 Slice 5
			6 - ODU1 Slice 6
			7 - ODU1 Slice 7
			8 - ODU1 Slice 8
			-----------------------------
			Values :
			If Alarm is Present - Date and Time Stamp
				    eg:2017-5-18,9:47:20.0,+5:30
			If Alarm is Absent  - 0
			-----------------------------"
		::= { ommp81PlusAlarmQueryEntry 130 }

	ommp81PlusOpuPayloadMismatchAlarm OBJECT-TYPE
              SYNTAX  DisplayString
              MAX-ACCESS  read-only
              STATUS  current
              DESCRIPTION
			"For port configured with OTU2/OTU1 traffic, 
			OPU-PLM Alarm is declared if the accepted payload type
			is not equal to the expected payload type.
			-----------------------------
			ommp81PlusInterfaceNumber:
